  {
   "source": "mcguffey g2 (Brown/winter)",
   "passage": "It is winter. The cold wind whistles through the branches of the trees. Brown has done his day work, and his children, Harry and Kate, have come home from school. They learned their lessons well to-day, and Tea is over. Brown has put the little sitting room in order. The fire burns brightly. One lamp gives light enough for all. On the stool is a basket of fine apples. Harry and Kate read a story in a new book. The father reads his newspaper, and the mother mends Harry stockings.",
